Feature: Mask the last four digits of invoice_number in d_product_revenue_clone table

  Background:
    Given a Databricks workspace with Unity Catalog "purgo_databricks"
    And schema "purgo_playground" exists
    And the table "purgo_playground.d_product_revenue" exists
    And the table "purgo_playground.d_product_revenue_clone" is dropped if it exists
    When the table "purgo_playground.d_product_revenue_clone" is created as a replica of "purgo_playground.d_product_revenue"

  Scenario: Successfully mask the last four digits of a valid invoice_number
    Given the "invoice_number" is "1234234534"
    When the masking process is executed
    Then the "invoice_number" should be "123423****"

  Scenario Outline: Masking various valid invoice_number formats
    Given the "invoice_number" is "<invoice_number>"
    When the masking process is executed
    Then the "invoice_number" should be "<expected_masked_invoice_number>"

    Examples:
      | invoice_number | expected_masked_invoice_number |
      | 9876543210     | 987654****                     |
      | 111122223333    | 11112222****                   |
      | 555566667777    | 55556666****                   |
      | 1234            | ****                            |

  Scenario: Handle invoice_number with fewer than four digits
    Given the "invoice_number" is "123"
    When the masking process is executed
    Then an error "invoice_number must have at least four digits" is thrown

  Scenario: Handle null invoice_number
    Given the "invoice_number" is null
    When the masking process is executed
    Then an error "invoice_number cannot be null" is thrown

  Scenario Outline: Verify data type consistency for invoice_number
    Given the "invoice_number" data type is "<data_type>"
    When the masking process is executed
    Then the data type of "invoice_number" remains "<data_type>"

    Examples:
      | data_type |
      | bigint    |
      | string    |

  Scenario: Verify masked invoice_number is loaded into d_product_revenue_clone
    Given the table "purgo_playground.d_product_revenue_clone" exists
    And the "invoice_number" column contains masked values
    When data is loaded into "purgo_playground.d_product_revenue_clone"
    Then all "invoice_number" entries have the last four digits masked with '*'

  Scenario: Validate invoice_number format after masking
    Given the "invoice_number" is "1234234534"
    When the masking process is executed
    Then the "invoice_number" should match the regex "^\d{6}\*{4}$"

  Scenario: Ensure no unintended columns are altered during masking
    Given the table "purgo_playground.d_product_revenue_clone" is replicated
    When the masking process is executed
    Then only the "invoice_number" column is modified

  Scenario: Confirm masking does not affect downstream systems
    Given the masking process updates "purgo_playground.d_product_revenue_clone"
    When downstream systems access "invoice_number"
    Then they receive the masked "invoice_number" without errors

  Scenario: Schedule the masking operation as a recurring job
    Given the masking operation needs to run daily
    When the PySpark script is scheduled
    Then it executes the masking process every 24 hours

  Scenario: Deploy the PySpark code within the Databricks environment
    Given the PySpark masking script is developed
    When it is deployed to the Databricks environment
    Then it integrates with existing CI/CD pipelines

  Scenario: Validate masked data meets acceptance criteria
    Given the invoice data is masked
    When data validation is performed
    Then all masked "invoice_number" entries comply with the masking rules
